~~ Canonical SoA kernel for the 400-particle proof harness.
~~
~~ The caller owns the stack's two contiguous float columns and its count
~~ (400 in the demo). The run replaces the position column, and the compiler
~~ visits the records one target-native rack at a time, handling a final
~~ partial rack when required.
pack Particles {
  f32: position_x, velocity_x;
}

run advance_x(particles: stack Particles, <dt: f32>) -> stack Particles:
  particles with { position_x: particles.position_x + particles.velocity_x * <dt> }
